.TH LRCGET 1 "1970-1-1" "v1.0" "Custom Scripts Manual"
.SH NAME
lrcget \- Fetches track lyrics from the LRCLIB API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lrcget
[\fB\-h\fR] [\fB\-m\fR \fImode\fR] \fB\-n\fR \fItrack_name\fR \fB\-a\fR \fIartist_name\fR \fB\-l\fR \fIalbum_name\fR \fB\-d\fR \fIduration\fR [\fB\-o\fR \fIoutput_file\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lrcget
is a command-line wrapper script that interfaces with the LRCLIB API to find, format, and extract song lyrics. The script requires both a track name and an artist name to complete a targeted lookup.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h
Show the help menu and exit.
.TP
.B \-m \fImode\fR
Specify the parsing structure and format requirements for returned output. Valid targets include:
.RS
.IP "\fBjson\fR" 12
Returns the raw JSON response payload from the API (default).
.IP "\fBsynced\fR" 12
Extracts timed LRC-formatted lyrics only.
.IP "\fBplain\fR" 12
Extracts plain text lyrics without timestamps.
.IP "\fBfallback\fR" 12
Attempts to extract synced lyrics first; if unavailable, falls back to plain text.
.RE
.TP
.B \-n \fItrack_name\fR
The title of the song track to look up (Required).
.TP
.B \-a \fIartist_name\fR
The name of the artist or band responsible for the track (Required).
.TP
.B \-l \fIalbum_name\fR
The name of the album associated with the track.
.TP
.B \-d \fIduration\fR
The precise song duration value represented as an integer of total seconds.
.TP
.B \-o \fIoutput_file\fR
Saves the processed output stream into the designated target file instead of redirecting it to stdout.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Failure due to missing metadata, invalid formatting flags, or invalid execution arguments.
.TP
.B 2
Target search returned no matching items (API 404).
.TP
.B 3
Network execution issues or arbitrary unexpected HTTP responses.
.TP
.B 4
The requested track entry exists, but lacks data matching the chosen formatting mode.
.SH EXAMPLE
.PP
.B lrcget \-m fallback \-n "Song" \-a "Artist" \-l "Album" \-d 360 \-o out.lrc
.RS
Queries a hypothetical song for lyrics (synced if not plain) and saves them to a file called out.lrc
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curl (1),
.BR jq (1)
